    __id: "5",
    name: "Char Dham Yatra from Pithoragarh (via Bageshwar)",
    overview:
      "Embark on one of India's most sacred pilgrimages, the 11-day Char Dham Yatra, from Pithoragarh. This spiritual journey takes you through the four revered shrines of Yamunotri, Gangotri, Kedarnath, and Badrinath, nestled in the majestic Himalayas. Following a scenic route via Bageshwar and Karnaprayag to avoid crowded roads, this tour offers a perfect blend of devotion, adventure, and breathtaking landscapes. Experience the divine aura of ancient temples, the purity of sacred rivers, and the tranquility of the Himalayan valleys on this comprehensive and spiritually fulfilling yatra.",
    description:
      "<h2>Sacred Pilgrimage Through the Himalayas</h2>\n<p>Join us for a divine <strong>11-day Char Dham Yatra</strong>, uniquely starting from Pithoragarh. This special itinerary is designed to take you on a scenic route via Bageshwar and Karnaprayag, consciously avoiding the crowded Haridwar road. This allows pilgrims to experience the tranquility of Himalayan valleys, the purity of sacred rivers, and the divine aura of ancient temples in a more serene and peaceful manner.</p>\n<p>Each of the four dhams holds immense spiritual significance, and this journey offers a profound opportunity to connect with your faith:</p>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>Yamunotri:</strong> The origin of the sacred River Yamuna. Here, devotees can take a holy dip in the hot springs of Surya Kund and offer prayers at the temple dedicated to Goddess Yamuna.</li>\n  <li><strong>Gangotri:</strong> The sacred source of the River Ganga (Bhagirathi). This site is revered for its pristine waters and deep mythological importance, marking the place where King Bhagirath performed penance.</li>\n  <li><strong>Kedarnath:</strong> Home to one of the 12 Jyotirlingas of Lord Shiva. This powerful shrine offers a mystical and transformative trekking experience, surrounded by snow-capped peaks.</li>\n  <li><strong>Badrinath:</strong> The divine abode of Lord Vishnu, this temple is one of the 108 Divya Desams. A visit to Badrinath marks the holy completion of the Char Dham pilgrimage.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>This tour is not just a journey; it's an experience that combines devotion with the awe-inspiring beauty of the Uttarakhand Himalayas. We provide comfortable travel, well-planned accommodation, and special assistance for senior travelers to ensure your pilgrimage is as seamless and spiritually rewarding as possible.</p>",
